<BlogPost
  title="Discontinued: Ironing Board 16 (IB-16) in Shiloh and Eclipse — Use the IB-18"
  description="W.W. Wood discontinued the IB-16 ironing board accessory in Shiloh and Eclipse effective July 29, 2026. Orders already in-house will be filled. The IB-18 is the substitute for 18″–21″ wide, 21″ or 24″ deep cabinets."
  author="Ben Miller"
  publishedDate="2026-07-29"
  ogImage="/images/blog/ib-16-ironing-board-discontinued/ib-16-discontinued.webp"
  heroImage="/images/blog/ib-16-ironing-board-discontinued/ib-16-discontinued.webp"
>

<p><strong>Effective July 29, 2026</strong>, W.W. Wood Products discontinued the <strong>Ironing Board 16 (SKU: IB-16)</strong> accessory in both <a href="/brands/shiloh-cabinetry/">Shiloh Cabinetry</a> and <a href="/brands/eclipse-cabinetry/">Eclipse Full Access Cabinetry</a>.</p>

<div class="post-figure">
  <img src="/images/blog/ib-16-ironing-board-discontinued/ib-16-discontinued.webp" alt="Discontinued notice for the IB-16 Ironing Board 16 accessory in Shiloh and Eclipse Cabinetry" width="1200" height="630" fetchpriority="high" />
</div>

<h2>What you need to know</h2>

<ul>
  <li><strong>Orders already in-house that include the IB-16 will still be fulfilled.</strong></li>
  <li><strong>No new orders containing the IB-16 are accepted</strong> as of July 29, 2026. If you have an open quote or a layout in progress with an IB-16, swap it before the order goes in.</li>
</ul>

<h2>The substitute: IB-18</h2>

<p>The <strong>IB-18 remains available</strong> and is the recommended replacement for a built-in ironing board. It fits:</p>

<ul>
  <li>Cabinets <strong>18″ – 21″ wide</strong></li>
  <li>Cabinets <strong>21″ or 24″ deep</strong></li>
</ul>

<p>If your laundry or mudroom layout used a 16″ cabinet for the IB-16, you'll need to widen that cabinet to at least 18″ to use the IB-18 — check the adjacent filler and appliance dimensions before you re-issue the drawing.</p>

<h2>Catalogs and design software</h2>

<p>The Shiloh and Eclipse Interactive PDF catalogs will be updated to reflect the change, along with other updates W.W. Wood will announce. <strong>2020 (Cyncly) Design and ProKitchen catalogs have not yet been updated</strong> — the IB-16 may still appear in your CAD software. Don't let it slip onto an order from an old drawing.</p>

<h2>Questions</h2>

<ul>
  <li><strong>Pinnacle Sales</strong> — send any affected job through <a href="/dealer-hub/submit/?type=order-check">Submit a Request</a> and we'll help rework the cabinet.</li>
  <li><strong>W.W. Wood Products customer service</strong> — <a href="tel:5736243526">573-624-3526, ext. 1153</a> or <a href="mailto:customer.service@wwinc.com">customer.service@wwinc.com</a>.</li>
</ul>

